00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:07.280
>> Okay, first, you're not coming from a

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:09.040
solution place. You must come from a

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:11.400
problem space. So, coming up with

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:13.080
problems. And then after you go for the

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:14.480
solution. Here you come up with

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:16.440
different hypotheses, different

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:18.480
solutions, and you design experiments to

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:20.240
test this hypothesis. So, first, what

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:21.560
problem am I solving? How do I know if

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:23.280
it's real? You must know if it's This is

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:25.120
happening. And then what's the solution

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:26.640
and the hypothesis? How much will each

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:28.400
hypothesis move the metric? Are there

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:30.040
any guardrail metrics I should watch

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:31.640
out? And then also very important, you

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:33.400
must AB test everything. You have your

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:35.440
control version, the version of your app

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:37.400
currently, and the new version being AB

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:39.400
