Here we have all of our AB test tracks.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:51.960
This is a database that comes from user

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:53.800
interviews. So, it's user interviews

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:55.400
that show us that user problem. Then we

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:57.160
do the hypothesis, and then we do the

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:58.960
experiment. These experiments are being

00:11:57.160 --> 00:12:00.480
tracked in Posthog. So, here we track

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:02.760
everything, and we can see how

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:04.120
everything is running. For example, this

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:05.720
